                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fb0517e5-668c-31dd-9d53-9ed7adbbe826",
                        "entry_id": "f039fd90-0039-392d-a92b-15f83b19f62c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To come together but fail to properly communicate or connect in positive ways."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0488204-42e3-49d5-b1d5-c6b66f974b32",
                                "sense_id": "fb0517e5-668c-31dd-9d53-9ed7adbbe826",
                                "text": "Crash is an ensemble film “varying in scope from an ensemble of characters who may meet or 'mismeet' in the same city or suburb” (Sim 2012, pp. 113)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6da15fba-249b-4634-96bd-fd4b3b2a06ed",
                                "sense_id": "fb0517e5-668c-31dd-9d53-9ed7adbbe826",
                                "text": "Perhaps more than any other it illustrates both the meeting and the mismeeting of religion and psychology."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "42c94c57-9c1a-47c2-8508-60648e71a929",
                                "sense_id": "fb0517e5-668c-31dd-9d53-9ed7adbbe826",
                                "text": "The noble task of the teacher is to be attentive to his students, in order not to 'mismeet' the graced occasions of dialogue, as already noted."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3791fe22-d302-4e9e-a4c2-ef73db1a46c4",
                                "sense_id": "fb0517e5-668c-31dd-9d53-9ed7adbbe826",
                                "text": "Have you ever tried to talk with a stranger — on a blind date or one-on-one with a business associate — but could not find the words? We mismeet in relatively superficial and trivial conditions as well as in crucial ones. When we mismeet, I can run only one side—my side—of the dialogue."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a261494-755e-4a0d-8ce3-25bafd856239",
                                "sense_id": "fb0517e5-668c-31dd-9d53-9ed7adbbe826",
                                "text": "There is scattered discussion of how society values different species of animals differently—specifically, companion animals, wild animals, and food animals. This classification is nearly identical to the one Zygmunt Bauman uses in his examination of how we treat nonpersons in our society: how pets are met and included in our society; how wild animals are unmet, recognized as animals but outside our society; and how food animals are mismet and evicted from society."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "524e855d-a0d2-3cde-bd27-316cb672f864",
                        "entry_id": "f039fd90-0039-392d-a92b-15f83b19f62c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To fail to properly satisfy or comply with."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5b5aaf2-83a1-4a0c-80f0-9989c5e3e5fc",
                                "sense_id": "524e855d-a0d2-3cde-bd27-316cb672f864",
                                "text": "In such pathological relatedness, the child's archaic security needs (which are developmentally immature and of a grandiose and idealizing nature) either go unmet or are mismet."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1986fe2-6d5e-45a1-95b6-c1cd92c00109",
                                "sense_id": "524e855d-a0d2-3cde-bd27-316cb672f864",
                                "text": "These may be typiﬁed by situations in which the affect, plan, expectancy, need state, communication, or other function of the baby is unmet or mismet by the parent or caregiver."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
